From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000006 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tab S9 FE Linux Project <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 13:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ANDROID: devfreq: reject a missing dfs_id safely

The fallback passes an uninitialized string pointer to
of_property_match_string() and does not store its return value.  All S5E8835
devfreq domains provide dfs_id, so fail cleanly when that required property is
absent instead of retaining an unusable and unsafe fallback.

Signed-off-by: Tab S9 FE Linux Project <noreply@example.invalid>
---
 drivers/devfreq/exynos/exynos-devfreq.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/devfreq/exynos/exynos-devfreq.c b/drivers/devfreq/exynos/exynos-devfreq.c
--- a/drivers/devfreq/exynos/exynos-devfreq.c
+++ b/drivers/devfreq/exynos/exynos-devfreq.c
@@ -1826,8 +1826,7 @@ static int exynos_devfreq_parse_dt(struct device_node *np, struct exynos_devfreq
 	if (of_property_read_u32(np, "pm_qos_class_max", &data->pm_qos_class_max))
 		return -ENODEV;
 
-	if (of_property_read_u32(np, "dfs_id", &data->dfs_id) &&
-			of_property_match_string(np, "clock-names", buf))
+	if (of_property_read_u32(np, "dfs_id", &data->dfs_id))
 		return -ENODEV;
 
 #if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_DEBUG_SNAPSHOT)
-- 
2.50.1
